      "role": "user",
      "content": "i finally ran a spectrum analysis on my aurasonics and i was right. there is definitely a low-frequency oscillation bleeding through that has nothing to do with audio playback. it feels so calculated. like they're intentionally trying to dull the edge of anyone who thinks differently. why would a company actually implement something like this? it feels like they're trying to standardize human thought by killing off creative neuro-divergence.",
